You can install GitHub CLI (gh) on macOS, Windows, or Linux using package managers like Homebrew, apt, winget, or by downloading binaries, then authenticate with gh auth login to start creating pull requests, managing issues, and repositories directly from your terminal. 

⚙️ Installation Methods
macOS

Homebrew: brew install gh

MacPorts: sudo port install gh

Conda: conda install gh --channel conda-forge

Direct download: .pkg installer from GitHub releases

Linux

Debian/Ubuntu: sudo apt install gh

Fedora/RHEL: sudo dnf install gh

openSUSE: sudo zypper install gh

Precompiled binaries: .deb, .rpm, .tar.gz from GitHub releases

Windows

Winget: winget install --id GitHub.cli

Scoop: scoop install gh

Chocolatey: choco install gh

MSI installer from GitHub releases

🔑 Authentication
After installation, run:

bash
gh auth login
Choose GitHub.com or your enterprise server.

Select HTTPS or SSH for Git operations.

Follow prompts to authenticate with your GitHub account.
